-The startup refusal for a local endpoint (`127.0.0.1`, LAN, Docker service names) says which window the server is serving and names the fix for any OpenAI-compatible server, not just Ollama: raise the server's context (llama.cpp `-c 64000`, vLLM `--max-model-len`, Ollama `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH`/Modelfile `num_ctx`) or set `model.ollama_num_ctx` in `config.yaml` to the window the server really serves (at least 64K). `model.ollama_num_ctx` is honoured on every local endpoint; only the automatic detection behind it uses Ollama's `/api/show`.
+The startup refusal for a local endpoint (`127.0.0.1`, LAN, Docker service names) says which window the server is serving and names the fix for any OpenAI-compatible server, not just Ollama: raise the server's context (llama.cpp `-c 64000`, vLLM `--max-model-len`, Ollama `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH`/Modelfile `num_ctx`) or set `model.ollama_num_ctx` in `config.yaml` to the window the server really serves (at least 64K). `model.ollama_num_ctx` is honoured on every self-hosted server Hermes recognizes (Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio); only the automatic detection behind it uses Ollama's `/api/show`. Any other route in the same config, such as a hosted API, Ollama Cloud or a `process://` provider, ignores it, including after `/model` or a fallback moves a session there.
 
 #### "Context limit: 2048 tokens" at startup
 
